  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 197,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Child who bleeds: EXCESSIVE or UNUSUAL, read against NEWBORN normals?",
   "lines": [
    "excessive: nosebleed > 10 min, gum bleeding, wide bruising, heavy menses · unusual: brain or joint bleed, umbilical stump, surgery (dental, circumcision)",
    "liver immature until 6 months: vitamin K factors, protein C, S low → prothrombin time (PT/INR) and activated partial thromboplastin time (aPTT) normally LONGER, worst if premature",
    "LIFE-THREATENING bleed, no diagnosis yet → fresh frozen plasma (most factors; little VIII, vWF, fibrinogen) · cryoprecipitate = VIII, vWF, XIII + fibrinogen"
   ]
  },
  {
